# Requirements for the Fuzzy Matcher
This file contains the requirements for the fuzzy matching service and a MCP server.

## The Goal
We need to build another set of api service + tool-exposing MCP server.
The service will provide a fuzzy search in two database tables: Customers and Products.
Each table will have just two columns : id and name.
The sevice will accept a call with two parameters:
- entity: either "product" or "customer"
- text: text to match the name (fuzzy matching)
The service will return a list of objects :
[
  { id: 1, name: "Product 1", confidence: 0.92}
]

## The Tech Stack
These services and the MNP Server will be built in Python.
We will use FastAPI for the API service and the MCP server will be built using the MCP Python SDK library.
From the Python stack we will use:
- FastAPI
- MCP Python SDK
- SQLAlchemy (the database will be MS SQL and will be provided by the environment)
- Pydantic
- Python 3.13
The services will be deployed in Docker containers to K8s / K3s cluster.
